-- statement:
--   The source lengths of §9.2.2 exist for `n ≥ n₀` (pairwise coprime odd `s_i` in the resampling windows of the axis lengths `r/2` or `r`).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.GlueParams`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.OpenAI.Glue.sources_ok {n : ℕ} (hn : n0 ≤ n) (d' : ℕ) (hd' : d' ≤ dP n) :
--       ∃ s : Fin (dP n) → ℕ, (∀ i, Odd (s i)) ∧ (∀ i j, i ≠ j → Nat.Coprime (s i) (s j)) ∧
--         ∀ i : Fin (dP n), (4 * dP n - 2) * (if (i : ℕ) < d' then rP n / 2 else rP n) < 4 * dP n * s i ∧
--           4 * dP n * s i ≤ (4 * dP n - 1) * (if (i : ℕ) < d' then rP n / 2 else rP n)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *Glue 3: explicit parameters `n ↦ (b, L, T, d, K, ℓ, α, p)` of §9.2 and the threshold `n₀`*: For an input length `n` (§9.2.1):
